      "validated": false,
      "notes": "Fastest local engine measured (sesame-class-voice-0y39 Wave-2: TTFB-audible 285 ms median, RTF 0.210, 6.2 GiB co-resident, true word-level streaming). CC-BY-4.0 weights: commercial use permitted WITH attribution (ship Kyutai credit + model-card link in distribution legal docs); moshi Python code is MIT. VOICE LIBRARY RULE: preset voices ship from voice-donations/ (CC0) or user-minted embeddings ONLY — expresso/* is CC-BY-NC (non-commercial), excluded at catalog-build time and refused by the sidecar allowlist. Download contract (kyutai-engine-phase1-srex S-2 spike; both repos pinned to the spike commits): the model repo is GATED — first fetch needs HF auth; the 4 pinned files are the COMPLETE load set (3.79 GiB). moshi loads them from the flat managed engine dir via explicit local-Path overrides — dir-as-repo-id raises HFValidationError, never do it. Voice embeddings are checkpoint-specific (suffix 1e68beda@240 from config.json model_id); the 8 curated CC0 donations (~250 KiB each) land under voice-donations/ in the same managed dir. n_q/temp are synthesis-time knobs, not registry fields. vramGb 7 = 6.2 GiB measured peak rounded up; diskGb 4 covers the 3.79 GiB model + voice set — verify at download. S-7 two-caller probe (kyutai-engine-phase1-srex wave-2, single global lock): caller B's first frame landed 285.3 ms after caller A's final frame, zero interleave — B waited 3719.4 ms behind a ~3.9 s turn. That head-of-line cost is the recorded evidence for the deferred NFR-8 LRU worker pool."
    },
