      "validated": true,
      "notes": "Two-checkpoint engine — Base (x-vector voice clone) + VoiceDesign (prose-described voice design) — BOTH loaded co-resident at startup: 8610 MiB measured (~8.6 GiB), inside the 16 GB budget with headroom; vramGb 9 rounds that up, diskGb 9 = 8.5 GB on disk for the two pinned snapshots. BATCH-ONLY: qwen-tts exposes no streaming path — full generation, then uniform 80 ms PCM chunks; first-audio TTFB scales ~0.05 s/char (design 0.0485, clone 0.0341 + ~0.8 s fixed, measured with llama-server co-resident), so turns must show GENERATING honestly, never a fake-live transport. Attention: sdpa is the CONFIRMED path — flash-attn absent on the rig (ImportError); real generations ran on sdpa on both checkpoints. Download layout: the two repos CANNOT share one flat dir (root filename collisions — config.json, model.safetensors), so each snapshots into its own managed subdir via targetSubdir (base/ + voice-design/), both pinned to the qwen3-engine-q3gh Wave-1 spike revs with the identical 11-file allow set. Clone is x-vector-only: the Base model serves NO preset voices (any voice id 400s fail-closed) and ref audio reaches the model only as a validated in-process (ndarray, sr) tuple — never as a path/URL string through qwen-tts's convenience loader (SSRF-shaped). Design mode REQUIRES an integer seed (0..2^31-1) — determinism is the design voice's identity. Language set from the model card (10 languages); Wave-1 generations proved English. validated:true flipped 2026-07-20 — the Wave-3 live suite passed 10/10 on the shipping path (engine-manager launch, clone+design renders, disconnect/watchdog/drain recoveries, 15/15 battery, clean shutdown), VoiceDesign determinism proven BITWISE across three renders, clone ECAPA 0.8032 vs the pre-registered 0.5 gate (margin 0.4876 vs 0.15)."
